# Server declarations

```rocci
@get:view("/") = |{ db }|
    counterPage({ count: count })
```

Route declarations use mandatory verb-first `@method:role("path")`
headers. The former role-first forms, `@on`, trailing `json`, and
pathless `@live` are **removed**, not aliases.

Bodies are Roc, not templates. Module-level only.

| Declaration | Success |
| --- | --- |
| `@context { … }` | `State` type; one per module |
| `@init { … }` | context value; `?` exits the process |
| `@get:view(path)` | HTML document |
| `@get:fragment(path)` | finite patch-elements response |
| `@get:live(path)` | long-lived fragment stream |
| `@post:fragment(path)` | finite patch-elements response |
| `@put:fragment(path)` | finite patch-elements response |
| `@patch:fragment(path)` | finite patch-elements response |
| `@delete:fragment(path)` | finite patch-elements response |
| `@post:command(path)` | no success representation |
| `@put:command(path)` | no success representation |
| `@patch:command(path)` | no success representation |
| `@delete:command(path)` | no success representation |

Dispatch calls `handler!(context, request)`. Write `|{ db }, request|` when
you read the request. One-parameter lists append `_request`. Omit params for
`|state, _request|`.

There are no default methods. Any method/role pair outside this closed matrix
is rejected. Paths are literal and app-wide method/path collisions are
rejected across the primary module and siblings. A module may declare multiple
live routes; each becomes one SSE endpoint. A page with exactly one local live
route and no authored `data-init` receives an automatic subscription. Multiple
local streams require explicit `data-init` subscriptions.

Complete matrix: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

**Related:** [Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/),
[Handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/).
